  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nIn `WHITELIST_ENABLED` state, `_beforeTokenTransfer` only checks that recipients are not blacklisted; it never requires `WHITELISTED_ROLE`/`whitelisted[to]` for minting or redemption. A whitelisted minter (e.g., issuer or adapter) can mint iTRY/iTryOFT directly to any non-whitelisted address, bypassing the whitelist gate that is supposed to restrict send/receive/burn to whitelisted users. This breaks compliance controls and allows sanctioned/unvetted addresses to hold and later transfer tokens once transfer state changes.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nIn the `WHITELIST_ENABLED` branch, require `WHITELISTED_ROLE` (or `whitelisted[to]`) for minting and redemption, mirroring the transfer checks. Enforce both sender and receiver whitelisting for all mint/burn paths when the whitelist state is active.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// forge test --match-path test/pocs/poc_whitelist_bypass.t.sol\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {ERC1967Proxy} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\nimport {iTry} from \"src/token/iTRY/iTry.sol\";\nimport {IiTryDefinitions} from \"src/token/iTRY/IiTryDefinitions.sol\";\n\ncontract WhitelistBypassPOC is Test {\n    iTry token;\n    address minter = address(0xBEEF);\n    address nonWhitelisted = address(0xCAFE);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        iTry impl = new iTry();\n        bytes memory initData = abi.encodeWithSelector(iTry.initialize.selector, address(this), minter);\n        ERC1967Proxy proxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(impl), initData);\n        token = iTry(address(proxy));\n        token.updateTransferState(IiTryDefinitions.TransferState.WHITELIST_ENABLED);\n    }\n\n    function test_MintBypassesWhitelist() public {\n        vm.prank(minter);\n        token.mint(nonWhitelisted, 1 ether); // succeeds though recipient is not whitelisted\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(nonWhitelisted), 1 ether, \"mint to unwhitelisted should be blocked\");\n    }\n}\n```",
